<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch4-chapter-model-and-monte-carlo" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Monte Carlo Simulation</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> 
      This chapter introduces students to the idea of building and simulating models in order to perform
      simulation-based inference. This chapter will also cover very basic probability ideas and will begin 
      to teach students how to summarize and describe distributions of quantitative data. There will also be an 
      introduction to sampling distributions, sampling variability, and standard error.  
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <objectives>
    <ol>
    <li>Explore ideas of randomness, which permeates, and is fundamental to statistics.</li>

    <li>Learn to model random processes and generate outcomes from these models/simulate data from these models.</li>

    <li>Summarize simulation results after generating multiple outcomes from the same model, which helps us to make sense of the process we are modeling.</li>

    <li>Use Monte Carlo simulation to estimate the probability of an event of interest occurring.</li>
  </ol>
  </objectives>
  
  <!-- include sections -->
  <xi:include href="section-ch4-simulation-intro.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="section-ch4-summarize-sim.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="section-ch4-sampling-dist.ptx" />

</chapter>





